F2.1 ac=scope at=tests/skills/test_mcp_proxy_names.py:23 anchor="every `tools:`/`allowed-tools:` line naming `mcp__tavily__tavily_<x>` also names `mcp__litellm__Tavily-tavily_<x>`" chk=n,n,n,n family=guard-yaml-list-blindspot fix=Optional hardening: also check YAML block-list allow-list entries (`  - mcp__tavily__tavily_<x>` under a `tools:` key) for a proxy twin on the preceding entry. Non-blocking. covers="every `tools:`/`allowed-tools:` line": `_TOOLS_LINE` only matches lines that begin with `tools:`/`allowed-tools:`, so the ten agents whose allow-lists are YAML block lists (for example src/superclaude/agents/rf-analyst.md:14, src/superclaude/agents/deep-research.md:7-13) are not covered by the Tavily check or the AUG-before-auggie ordering check. The brief's literal "line" wording is met and those agents are compliant today (each carries its `- mcp__litellm__Tavily-...` twin), so this is a coverage gap for future regressions, not an AC miss.
